# Heavy media stays OUT of git (the repo is public and git stores every binary version forever).
# Everything ignored here is listed in docs/MEDIA.md (size, duration, sha256) so an agent knows it exists,
# and docs/HISTORY.md explains how each piece was made. Regenerate MEDIA.md with: python tools/media_manifest.py

# --- client source footage (private client material) ---
raw-footags/

# --- finished renders / deliverables (share via Drive or similar) ---
outputs/*.mp4
outputs/*.mov
projects/*/renders/

# --- regenerable intermediates ---
# Pukhtoon: tools/build_base.py -> base-vN.mp4, music trims from voice/restraunt/
projects/pakhtoon-vid-1/assets/base-*.mp4
projects/pakhtoon-vid-1/assets/music-*.wav
# ZELECTRONICS: tools/make_audio.py -> audio.wav
projects/*/assets/audio.wav
*.tmp.wav

# --- HyperFrames local state, snapshots, check reports ---
**/.hyperframes/

# --- third-party content (other people's reels, commercial music) ---
refrences/**/*.mp4
refrences/**/frames/
voice/restraunt/
voice/ref-*/*.wav

# --- tooling noise ---
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
